  "interpretation": {
    "DESCRIPTIVE_ONLY": "n=18 languages. Protocol s7 forbids treating these as inferential or causal.",
    "pool_bias": "unjudged@10 correlates strongly negatively with resource volume (rho -0.660): low-resource languages have far more of their top-10 unjudged, so their nDCG is deflated by a benchmark property, not a system property. ISSUE-007.",
    "reference_validity": "BM25 nDCG@10 shows essentially NO association with pretraining resource volume (rho -0.059). This is the behaviour the identification strategy assumes: BM25 has no pretrained parameters, so it should not track pretraining volume. Measured rather than assumed.",
    "consequence": "If a dense encoder DOES show a resource association, that contrast is informative precisely because the pretraining-free reference does not. It does not by itself license causal attribution."
  }
